      "side": 1,
      "message": "I would move `constants` up to the beginning of the `preserved_ring_buf_t` struct, so the memory allocated for the buffer starts with constants as a \"header\" and has the length (capacity) before the data. It would also make checksum to serve as a canary, in case the beginning of `preserved_ring_buf_t` is damaged for some reason - the checksum (the very first field in the struct) will be invalid.",
